+Publishing a stage replaces it and detaches the stages that depended on it. Every
+`apply` and `stage` call returns a new `StageResult` whose `info`, `recipe` and `model`
+were captured when it was created: its model is its own, so changing it affects nothing
+else, and it stays usable after its stage is replaced. Every inference snapshot is
+repaired for its monotone constraints; later stages use a separately retained working
+bank so the sequence agrees with ordinary one-call fitting.
+
+Use `pruning_selection(Prune(...))` to inspect an automatic recommendation or manual rule
+without building a model, and `pruning_budgets(Prune(...))` for the default schedule of
+table budgets. For a new fit or evaluation fold, `new_session.apply(recipe)` replays the
+policy against that fit's own evidence, rather than transferring support sets from
+another fit; it publishes nothing unless every operation succeeds.
+`recipe.to_plain_data()` and `Recipe.from_plain_data(...)` are its strict JSON form.
 
