-linearly, so no candidate exceeds the configured maxima. Numeric and categorical setup,
-master cuts and prefix sums are shared; each candidate calibrates independently.
-
-Smoothing's default multipliers are 0.25, 0.5, 1, 2 and 4, plus a configured Auto multiplier
-if it differs. Table decompositions and pre-guard proposals are shared. Higher-order
-smoothing stays fixed at the configured `high_order_alpha` for every positive point.
-Manual alpha follows the ordinary direct-solve policy. Reports distinguish proposed,
-requested and applied alpha; a global training guard rejection retains the original bank.
-EDF is measured before final constraints and reanchoring. These library diagnostics are
